-- title:
--   Lemma EC.4 — admissible strategies in $X$ and in the numéraire assets $N$ correspond, and $\pi_T(\mathcal A_N)=\chi_T(\mathcal A_X)/Z^M_T$
-- statement:
--   Throughout, the standing model of §3.1 holds: $B,\tilde B$ independent Brownian motions with augmented filtrations $\mathcal F\supseteq\mathcal G$, the asset $dX_t=X_t(\mu_t\,dt+\sigma_t\,dB_t)$, the demand component $C$ with $A_T=C_T+\tilde\sigma\tilde B_T$, the two Markov hypotheses, and $\mathbb P^M$ with $d\mathbb P^M/d\mathbb P=Z_T$ (12).
--
--   Suppose Assumptions 4–5 hold, and let $\zeta$ be a $\mathcal G$-adapted integrand of $dZ^M_t=\zeta_t\,dX_t$ (16), which drives the numéraire assets $N=(N^0,N^1)$ and the gains $\pi_t(\varphi)=\int_0^t\varphi\cdot dN$.
--
--   1. For every $\vartheta=\{\theta_t\}\in\mathcal A_X$ there is $\varphi=\{(\varphi^0_t,\varphi^1_t)\}\in\mathcal A_N$ with $\chi_t(\vartheta)/Z^M_t=\pi_t(\varphi)$ for all $t\in[0,T]$ and $\varphi_t=(\chi_t(\vartheta)-\theta_tX_t,\ \theta_t)$.
--   2. Conversely, for every $\varphi\in\mathcal A_N$ there is $\vartheta\in\mathcal A_X$ with $\chi_t(\vartheta)/Z^M_t=\pi_t(\varphi)$ for all $t\in[0,T]$ and $\theta_t=\zeta_t\big(\pi_t(\varphi)-\varphi_t\cdot N_t\big)+\varphi^1_t$.
--   3. Combining both, $\pi_T(\mathcal A_N)=\chi_T(\mathcal A_X)/Z^M_T=\{\chi_T(\vartheta)/Z^M_T:\ \vartheta\in\mathcal A_X\}$.
--
--   This turns problem (14) into a projection problem in the numéraire market, solved in the proof of Theorem 1.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: $\mathcal F_t$ and $\mathcal G_t$ are the filtrations generated by $(B_t,\tilde B_t)$ and $B_t$ (p.11) → the $\mathbb P$-augmented natural filtrations of $(B,\tilde B)$ and of $B$; reason: martingale representation (Prop. EC.3) holds for the augmented Brownian filtration, and null-set modifications of an adapted process must stay adapted
--   - reading: $(X_t,\mu_t,\sigma_t)$ is Markovian under $\mathbb P$ and $(X_t,\sigma_t)$ is Markovian under $\mathbb P^M$ (pp.11–12) → the simple Markov property on $[0,T]$ with respect to $\mathcal F$: $\mathbb E_Q[g(Y_t)\mid\mathcal F_s]=\mathbb E_Q[g(Y_t)\mid\sigma(Y_s)]$ a.s. for $s\le t\le T$ and bounded measurable $g$; reason: the paper does not define the term; this is the standard definition, relative to the filtration of footnote 4
--   - reading: $c$ the unit production cost, $s$ the unit salvage value, $X_0$ an asset price → $s<c$ and $x_0>0$ in the parameter structure; reason: the newsvendor convention (p.7), implied by Assumption 3 wherever it is assumed; $X_t>0$ is used on p.ec28
--   - encoding: processes on $[0,T]$ → processes indexed by $\mathbb R_{\ge0}$, constrained only for $t\le T$; reason: Mathlib's Brownian motion lives on $\mathbb R_{\ge0}$; values after $T$ never enter
--   - encoding: stochastic integrals $\int\theta\,dX$, $\int b\,d\tilde B$, $\int\eta\,dB$ with almost-sure integrability → the published relation `EthierKurtz.HasBrownianItoIntegral` (integrand cut off after $T$, square integrable on every path) plus a pathwise $du$-integral of the drift on every path; reason: under the augmented filtration an integrand can be set to zero on the exceptional null set without losing measurability, so the classes agree up to indistinguishability
--   - reading: for $u\le v$, $C_v-C_u$ is adapted to the σ-algebra generated by $\{X_t,u\le t\le v\}$ (p.11) → $C_v-C_u$ is measurable with respect to $\sigma\{X_t:u\le t\le v\}$, for $u\le v\le T$; reason: "adapted" for a single random variable means measurable
--   - encoding: $Z_t=e^{-\int_0^t\eta_s dB_s-\frac12\int_0^t\eta_s^2ds}$ (12) → $Z_t=\exp(-I_t-\frac12\int_0^t\eta_u^2du)$ with $I$ a $\mathcal G$-adapted version of the Itô integral $\int\eta\,dB$; reason: an Itô integral is fixed only up to a null set; the paper uses that $Z$ is $\mathcal G$-adapted (p.ec23)
--   - encoding: "martingale" (relative to $\mathcal F_t$, footnote 4) → `IsMartingaleOn`: adapted, integrable, and the martingale identity for $s\le t\le T$; reason: the paper's martingales live on $[0,T]$; Mathlib's `Martingale` constrains all times
--   - encoding: "adapted" integrands $a,b,\gamma,\xi,\delta,\zeta$ → progressively measurable integrands; reason: the standard measurability of a stochastic integrand; on an augmented filtration an adapted process has a progressive modification
--   - encoding: $\pi_t(\varphi)=\int_0^t\varphi^0dN^0+\int_0^t\varphi^1dN^1$ against the semimartingales $N^0,N^1$ → the integral defined through the dynamics (EC.7.12), $dN=(\ldots)\,dB^R$, written under $\mathbb P$ with $dB^R=dB+(\eta-\psi N^0)dt$, over progressive versions of the coefficients; reason: the paper derives (EC.7.12) from $dZ^M=\zeta\,dX$; the semimartingale decomposition is unique, so nothing depends on the representing $\zeta$; the coefficients contain the conditional expectation $Z^M_t$, fixed separately for each $t$, so the integrals run over progressive versions equal to them for a.e. $t$, a.s.
--   - encoding: "for all $t\in[0,T]$" and the formulas for $\varphi_t$, $\theta_t$ → a.s. equality for each $t\le T$; the integrand formulas hold for a.e. $t\in[0,T]$, a.s.; reason: integrands are determined only up to $dt\otimes d\mathbb P$-null sets
--   - encoding: the set equality (iii) → two inclusions, each up to almost-sure equality of terminal values; reason: random variables are identified up to null sets
--   - reading: $\zeta_t$ "defined in (16)" → any $\mathcal G$-progressive $\zeta$ with $Z^M_t=Z^M_0+\int_0^t\zeta\,dX$; reason: every such $\zeta$ is covered
--   - encoding: an admissible strategy $\vartheta=\{\theta_t\}$ with $\chi_t(\vartheta)=\int_0^t\theta_s dX_s$ (EC.7.15) → a pair $(\theta,\chi)$ with $\chi$ an $\mathcal F$-adapted version of the gains on $[0,T]$; reason: the stochastic integral is fixed only up to null sets, so the strategy is carried with its gains; the terminal gains are the same random variable a.s.
-- source:
--   Wang–Yao–Zhang, How Does Risk Hedging Impact Operations? Insights from a Price-Setting Newsvendor Model, arXiv:2201.01026v4, Lemma EC.4, p.ec31 (PDF 67); (EC.7.11)–(EC.7.18), pp.ec28–ec30

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_HedgePSNV_Numeraire

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

namespace HedgePSNV

/-- Lemma EC.4, arXiv:2201.01026v4, p.ec31: suppose Assumptions 4–5, and let `ζ` be the
integrand in `dZ^M_t = ζ_t dX_t` (16).
(i) For any `X_t`-admissible strategy `ϑ = {θ_t} ∈ A_X` there is an `N_t`-admissible strategy
`φ = {(φ⁰_t, φ¹_t)} ∈ A_N` with `χ_t(ϑ)/Z^M_t = π_t(φ)` for all `t ∈ [0, T]` and
`φ_t = (χ_t(ϑ) − θ_tX_t, θ_t)`.
(ii) Conversely, for any `φ ∈ A_N` there is `ϑ ∈ A_X` with `χ_t(ϑ)/Z^M_t = π_t(φ)` for all
`t ∈ [0, T]` and `θ_t = ζ_t(π_t(φ) − φ_t · N_t) + φ¹_t`.
(iii) Combining (i) and (ii), `π_T(A_N) = χ_T(A_X)/Z^M_T := {χ_T(ϑ)/Z^M_T : ϑ ∈ A_X}`.

Strategies are carried with their gains processes. The four conjuncts are (i), (ii), and the
two inclusions of (iii).

**Formalization Note** Equalities of random variables are almost sure, for each `t ≤ T`; the
formulas for `φ` and `θ` hold for almost every `t ∈ [0, T]`, almost surely (integrands are
determined only up to `dt ⊗ dP`-null sets). (iii) is an equality of sets of random variables
up to almost sure equality. `ζ` is any `G`-progressive integrand representing `Z^M`, as given
by Corollary EC.3. -/
theorem lemma_ec_4 (p : Params) {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (M : Model p Ω)
    (hM : M.Standing) (h4 : M.Assumption4) (h5 : M.Assumption5)
    (ζ χζ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) (hζ : IsStronglyProgressive M.G ζ) (hχζ : M.IsXGains ζ χζ)
    (hrepZ : ∀ t : ℝ≥0, t ≤ p.T → M.ZM t =ᵐ[M.P] fun ω => M.ZM0 + χζ t ω) :
    (∀ θ χ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ, (θ, χ) ∈ M.AX → ∃ φ0 π : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ,
      ((φ0, θ), π) ∈ M.AN ζ ∧
      (∀ t : ℝ≥0, t ≤ p.T → (fun ω => χ t ω / M.ZM t ω) =ᵐ[M.P] π t) ∧
      ∀ᵐ u ∂(volume.restrict (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) (p.T : ℝ))), ∀ᵐ ω ∂M.P,
        φ0 u.toNNReal ω = χ u.toNNReal ω - θ u.toNNReal ω * M.X u.toNNReal ω) ∧
    (∀ φ0 φ1 π : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ, ((φ0, φ1), π) ∈ M.AN ζ → ∃ θ χ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ,
      (θ, χ) ∈ M.AX ∧
      (∀ t : ℝ≥0, t ≤ p.T → (fun ω => χ t ω / M.ZM t ω) =ᵐ[M.P] π t) ∧
      ∀ᵐ u ∂(volume.restrict (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) (p.T : ℝ))), ∀ᵐ ω ∂M.P,
        θ u.toNNReal ω = ζ u.toNNReal ω * (π u.toNNReal ω -
          (φ0 u.toNNReal ω * M.N0 u.toNNReal ω + φ1 u.toNNReal ω * M.N1 u.toNNReal ω)) +
          φ1 u.toNNReal ω) ∧
    (∀ φ0 φ1 π : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ, ((φ0, φ1), π) ∈ M.AN ζ → ∃ θ χ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ,
      (θ, χ) ∈ M.AX ∧ π p.T =ᵐ[M.P] fun ω => χ p.T ω / M.ZM p.T ω) ∧
    (∀ θ χ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ, (θ, χ) ∈ M.AX → ∃ φ0 φ1 π : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ,
      ((φ0, φ1), π) ∈ M.AN ζ ∧ π p.T =ᵐ[M.P] fun ω => χ p.T ω / M.ZM p.T ω) := by sorry

end HedgePSNV
